<div id="2026-11-18-ency-startup-apkdownload" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-18 — ency :4011 would not start (missing Comserv::Util::ApkDownload)</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> <code>perl script/comserv_server.pl -p 4011 -r</code> forked its serving child, the child died immediately, and nothing ever bound port 4011. The process tree showed the <code>-r</code> supervisor alive with one un-reaped zombie child and no listener; <code>application.log</code> ended on a healthy health-evaluator line because the death happened during component load, before any request.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Api.pm</code> in this worktree carries the Android-Studio artifact line <code>use Comserv::Util::ApkDownload;</code>, but <code>Comserv::Util::ApkDownload</code> only exists on <code>main</code> (added there with the APK download endpoint). The ency branch is 61 commits behind <code>main</code>, so the module is absent here and Catalyst aborts while setting up the controllers:</p>
<p class="doc-body"><code>Can't locate Comserv/Util/ApkDownload.pm in @INC ... at lib/Comserv/Controller/Api.pm line 18. BEGIN failed--compilation aborted.</code></p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Fix.</strong> Restored the <code>main</code>-tracked copy of the module into this worktree (<code>git show main:… &gt; lib/Comserv/Util/ApkDownload.pm</code>). All 502 Controller/Model/View modules then load clean, the <code>-r</code> supervisor re-forked on the file event, and <code>http://127.0.0.1:4011/</code> answers 200.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Util/ApkDownload.pm</code> (restored from <code>main</code>). Follow-up: merge <code>main</code> into <code>ency</code> so the branch stops missing main-side modules.</p>
</div>
